IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Apportionment Act 1928 (Singapore) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Facts a witness could give about a periodical payment and the event that
-- splits it. Whether the payment is "apportionable", how much has accrued and
-- when it is payable are rules, in aa-act.l4.
--
-- Source: ../source/AA1928.txt (SSO PDF, current version as at 05 Oct 2026).

§ `Apportionment Act 1928 — the nouns`

-- s 2 and s 3 name four kinds of payment. A payment that is none of them —
-- a lump sum, a price, a one-off fee — is the fifth kind.
DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `rent`                                           -- s 2 "rents": incl. periodical payments or renderings in lieu of or in the nature of rent
    `annuity`                                        -- s 2 "annuities": incl. salaries and pensions
    `dividend`                                       -- s 2 "dividends"
    `another periodical payment in the nature of income`   -- s 3
    `a payment that is not periodical income`

-- s 4(a)-(b): is the payment still running, or has it come to an end?
DECLARE `State of the payment` IS ONE OF
    `continuing`                                                -- s 4(a)
    `determined by re-entry, death or otherwise`                -- s 4(b)

DECLARE Payment HAS
    `kind`                                              IS A `Kind of payment`
    `a return or reimbursement of capital`              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2 "dividends": excluded
    `an annual sum payable under a policy of assurance` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 6
    `expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7
    `state`                                             IS A `State of the payment`
    `amount of the entire portion`                      IS A NUMBER    -- dollars
    `accrual period begins`                             IS A DATE      -- for a dividend, the period "for or in respect of which" it is declared (s 2)
    `accrual period ends`                               IS A DATE
    `entire portion due on`                             IS A DATE      -- when the entire portion "becomes due and payable" (s 4(a)), or would have (s 4(b))
    `reserved out of or charged on lands or tenements`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(2)
    `just allowances against the entire portion`        IS A NUMBER    -- s 5(1) "allowing proportionate parts of all just allowances"

-- s 5(1): who has the remedies.
DECLARE Claimant IS ONE OF
    `the person entitled`
    `an executor, administrator or assign of the person entitled`
    `an executor, administrator or assign of a person whose interest determined with their death`
    `someone else`

-- The answers the Act gives (used by aa-act.l4).
DECLARE `Apportionment outcome` IS ONE OF
    `apportioned`  HAS `the apportioned part` IS A NUMBER
                       `payable on`          IS A DATE
                       `under`               IS A STRING
    `not apportionable: not periodical income within s 3`
    `not apportionable: a return or reimbursement of capital (s 2)`
    `not apportionable: an annual sum under a policy of assurance (s 6)`
    `not apportionable: apportionment expressly excluded (s 7)`

DECLARE `Route of recovery` IS ONE OF
    `the same remedies as for the entire portion`                                          -- s 5(1)
    `by suit against the person entitled to the entire rent, not against the tenant or the land`   -- s 5(2)
